ation of the data set has the value $x=11$ and $z$-score $z=0.8.$ Find the mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ of the data set.\n\n$\\overset{―}{x}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533813 true] [17592186253042 1113 #uuid "330c58a6-167a-5927-8488-a9c368002278" 13194139533813 true] [17592186253042 1145 "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=11,$ $z=0.8,$ and $\\sigma =2.5$ into the formula and solving for $\\overset{―}{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 11 & =\\overset{―}{x}+0.8\\cdot 2.5 \\\\ 11 & =\\overset{―}{x}+2 \\\\ \\overset{―}{x} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533813 true] [17592186253043 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253044 13194139533813 true] [17592186253043 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533813 true] [17592186253043 1041 "field-1" 13194139533813 true] [17592186253043 1104 #edb/ref 17592186253044 13194139533813 true] [17592186253043 1110 #uuid "16413860-6879-5ac8-95ec-a5dd6c7e36b0" 13194139533813 true] [17592186253044 1034 "9" 13194139533813 true] [17592186253044 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533813 true] [17592186253044 1111 #uuid "14a34250-6060-5154-be0e-418e556f9cb3" 13194139533813 true] [17592186253045 1017 #edb/ref 17592186253046 13194139533813 true] [17592186253045 1089 "q-332047" 13194139533813 true] [17592186253045 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533813 true] [17592186253045 1100 "A data set has a mean $\\overset{―}{x}=10$ and an unknown standard deviation. An observation of the data set has the value $x=12.1$ and $z$-score $z=1.05.$ Find the standard deviation of the data set.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533813 true] [17592186253045 1113 #uuid "26bebcb6-0fc4-55f8-8377-c7bba785f83f" 13194139533813 true] [17592186253045 1145 "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in